solutions.body:
The rule says $a_n=a_{n-1}a_{n+1}-1$, so $a_{n+1}= rac{a_n+1}{a_{n-1}}$. Starting from $x,2000$:

$$x,\ 2000,\  rac{2001}{x},\  rac{x+2001}{2000x},\  rac{x+1}{2000},\ x,\ 2000,\dots$$

(check: $ rac{(x+1)/2000+1}{(x+2001)/(2000x)}=x$). So only these five terms occur. $2001$ appears if

- $x=2001$;
- $ rac{2001}{x}=2001$: $x=1$;
- $ rac{x+2001}{2000x}=2001$: $x= rac{2001}{4001999}$;
- $ rac{x+1}{2000}=2001$: $x=4001999$.

These are four different positive values.

**Answer: (D) 4**
